      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the common difference of an arithmetic sequence if its fourth and fifth terms are $1$ and $7$, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *increasing*, and therefore we expect the common difference $d$ to be *positive*.\n\nSince the two terms are consecutive, we can find the common difference by subtracting ${a}_{4}$ from ${a}_{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{5}-{a}_{4} \\\\  & =7-1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=6.$",
