      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the common difference of an arithmetic sequence if its seventh and twenty-second terms are $126$ and $-9$, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{7}=126,\\,{a}_{22}=-9.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=22$ and $m=7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{22}-{a}_{7}}{22-7} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)-126}{22-7} \\\\  & =\\frac{-135}{15} \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-9.$",
